From the fluid files dev/fluids/{Krypton, Xenon, NitrousOxide, CarbonMonoxide, SulfurDioxide,
HydrogenSulfide, Ethane}.json (master, fetched 2026-10-14), these values are copied into
crates/hyperion-sim/src/substance/rows/diagrams.rs: the critical and triple points, the
coefficients of the ancillary vapour-pressure (pS) and saturated-liquid-density (rhoL) equations,
the triple-point states' pressures and the enthalpy of vaporisation they give, and ethane's
melting equation. The equations of state they rest on are Lemmon and Span 2006, Gao et al. 2016 and
Bücker and Wagner 2006, cited in that file.

From the same fetch's dev/fluids/{Methane, Nitrogen, Ethane, Ammonia, CarbonDioxide}.json, the
residual Helmholtz energies' coefficients and exponents of Setzmann and Wagner 1991, Span et al.
2000, Bücker and Wagner 2006, Gao et al. 2023 and Span and Wagner 1996 are copied into
crates/hyperion-sim/src/substance/rows/equations.rs, and their surface_tension ancillaries'
coefficients (Mulero, Cachadiña and Parra 2012) into crates/hyperion-sim/src/substance/rows/
liquids.rs (galaxy plan 14, P14.T49.h's second step), each cited there.

From the same five files, the ideal-gas parts' coefficients (alpha0: the logarithmic, power and
Planck-Einstein terms) of the same equations are copied into
crates/hyperion-sim/src/substance/rows/equations.rs, for the saturated liquids' specific heats
(rendering plan R09, R09.T13.i), each cited there.

